cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software when using VENUS."
type: software
title: "Vlasov–Einstein NUmerical Solver (VENUS)"
version: 1.0.0
license: BSD-3-Clause
authors:
  - given-names: Uddipan
    family-names: Banik
  - given-names: Frank C.
    family-names: van den Bosch
  - given-names: Sachiet
    family-names: Kapur
abstract: >-
  VENUS evolves distributions of collisionless and weakly collisional matter
  under spherical symmetry. It includes Einstein–Vlasov evolution in
  Schwarzschild and ingoing Eddington–Finkelstein coordinates, Newtonian
  Vlasov–Poisson and Boltzmann–Poisson evolution, weighted particle-in-cell
  methods, grid methods, and spherical direct simulation Monte Carlo.
keywords:
  - Einstein–Vlasov
  - Vlasov–Poisson
  - Boltzmann–Poisson
  - dark matter halos
  - black holes
